{"action":"final","query":{"op":"none","id":null,"start":null,"end":null,"search":null,"groupBy":null},"diagnosis":"getLiveIntervals follows descriptor views but stops at arith.select, so backing allocations can expire before the selected descriptor's load. In case-24/25, the temporary occupies columns [0,64), overlapping both selected candidates; all selected outputs become 7 (fact-24/26). With a 32-column temporary, only the candidate at column 0 is overwritten: case-27 fails while case-26 passes (fact-29/27). Early allocation avoids overlap and passes (case-30/31, fact-33/35). The repair transitively merges select-result liveness, including chained selects and intervening views, with a visited set to avoid repeated traversal at converging paths. It preserves first-fit placement, alignment, row constraints, and reuse after actual last use; the direct-first control's reuse of the dead second allocation remains legal (case-32, fact-36/37). Limitations: static IR does not establish GPU timestamps; compilation and runtime validation of this proposed edit were unavailable.","locations":[{"source_id":"source-01","start_line":120,"end_line":135},{"source_id":"source-02","start_line":17,"end_line":26},{"source_id":"source-03","start_line":15,"end_line":24},{"source_id":"source-05","start_line":17,"end_line":26},{"source_id":"source-06","start_line":16,"end_line":22},{"source_id":"source-08","start_line":18,"end_line":32}],"evidence_ids":["case-24","case-25","fact-24","fact-25","fact-26","case-26","case-27","fact-27","fact-28","fact-29","case-30","case-31","fact-33","fact-34","fact-35","case-32","fact-36","fact-37","case-36","fact-42","fact-43"],"edits":[{"old":"  // Merge the alloc liverange with the liverange of any subview of the
  // allocation.
  SmallVector<Operation *> users(value.getUsers());
  while (!users.empty()) {
    Operation *user = users.pop_back_val();
    if (!user->hasTrait<OpTrait::MemDescViewTrait>())
      continue;
    auto usersLivness = liveness.resolveLiveness(user->getResult(0));
    liveOperations.insert(liveOperations.end(), usersLivness.begin(),
                          usersLivness.end());
    users.append(user->getResult(0).getUsers().begin(),
                 user->getResult(0).getUsers().end());
  }
","new":"  // Merge the alloc liverange with the liveranges of descriptors that may
  // alias it through views or selects, including chains of these operations.
  SmallVector<Operation *> users(value.getUsers());
  DenseSet<Operation *> seen;
  while (!users.empty()) {
    Operation *user = users.pop_back_val();
    if (!seen.insert(user).second)
      continue;
    if (!user->hasTrait<OpTrait::MemDescViewTrait>() &&
        !isa<arith::SelectOp>(user))
      continue;
    auto usersLivness = liveness.resolveLiveness(user->getResult(0));
    liveOperations.insert(liveOperations.end(), usersLivness.begin(),
                          usersLivness.end());
    users.append(user->getResult(0).getUsers().begin(),
                 user->getResult(0).getUsers().end());
  }
"}]}
